# Project detail videos

All case-page **gallery** videos (pairs under the gallery, process clips) follow this stack. Use `ProjectFallbackVideo` + `ProtectedVideo` — do not invent a one-off player.

## Index card cover ≠ detail media

When the user supplies a **projects homepage / filter card cover** (`coverImage`):

- Wire it **only** to the index / featured / masonry card.
- **Do not** put that image on the project detail page as `heroImage`, `galleryLeadImage`, or any gallery still.
- Detail **hero video** and **all detail photos** are supplied separately — wait for those assets; do not invent or reuse the card cover.

`ProjectCaseDemo` must not fall back from missing gallery lead to `coverImage`.

## 0. First-screen hero background

Case detail hero prefers self-hosted `heroVideo` (+ optional `heroVideoStart` / `heroVideoEnd`) via `HeroSegmentVideo` + `ProtectedVideo`. YouTube (`heroYoutubeId`) only when no CDN file yet. Still: `heroImage` only when the user gives a dedicated detail still (never the index card). Do not invent a CDN fallback.

## 1. Sources

1. **Primary (原链接)** — if the user gives a TikTok / external original URL, wire it as `primary` first.
2. **Fallback (备用)** — only when they provide a CDN / direct mp4. Do **not** invent or scrape a fallback.
3. Until a fallback exists, keep `fallback` omitted / empty; the player stays on the primary and shows loading (or fails honestly) — do not silently swap to unrelated media.

Playback requirements on the working source: **muted**, **autoplay**, **loop**, **no download** (`ProtectedVideo`).

## 2. Cover before play

- **Loading only** — site mark (`VideoLoadingCover`) only while on-screen and not yet revealed. Loop full outlines; on playable → finish stroke → **slower fill** → unveil. **No black waiting plate.** Plate when showing is **pure black** (`#000`). Cover is `pointer-events: none`.
- **Hero first, then visibility + concurrency** — `lib/videoLoadQueue.ts`: page hero is absolute first (nothing else attaches during first load / home `edx-loading`). Unlock after hero **playing** (still onLoad / YouTube ready / hard fail). Routes **without** a page hero (Services, Thoughts, …) unlock the gate almost immediately — do not leave covers on a black plate for the long home failsafe. Then up to **2** near-viewport clips concurrently; prefer in-view over near; far clips stay without `src`. Scroll reorders **pending** work only — never revoke an active playing clip’s src. Gallery stills use `useNearViewportMedia` after hero.
- **Cover cards (Services / Insights / index)** use `CoverLoopVideo` with the **same** `VideoLoadingCover` mark as project clips. Show the mark as soon as the cell is on-screen — even while waiting for a queue slot — so users never stare at empty black.
- **Play when ready (background OK)** — once a gallery clip is allowed + buffered enough, `play()` immediately — **do not** wait for scroll-into-view. Mark loader is only for on-screen first paint; off-screen clips unveil quietly when settled. Synced pairs: left then right attach, then start together as soon as both are ready.
- **Layout stability** — gallery / pair cells always reserve height via `padding-bottom` ratio (including `nativeAspect`, which only switches to `object-fit: contain`). Do not use `height: auto` that collapses the box before metadata — that caused scroll jump/flash (fixed).
- **Home intro** — only home hero under the veil; intro completes on hero playable (+ fonts), no other-page waits. Failures unlock the page gate so the queue cannot deadlock.
- Soften `preload` after settle so “playing” doesn’t keep the network wide open forever.
- **Do not** extract a frame, generate a poster image, or invent a still from the video.
- Applies to case hero (`HeroSegmentVideo`), gallery clips (`ProjectFallbackVideo`), YouTube hero veil, home hero, and footer underlay.

## 3. Layout

Closing unboxing / social clips sit as a **two-column pair** at the **bottom** of the media stack (`endVideoPair` on the project), left | right, same gutter language as image pairs.

Full-width process clips go via `afterCoverVideo`. When `afterCoverStills` is set (e.g. frames 6–8 in one row), order is: cover still → stills row → process video → rest of gallery.
